  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The investment grant is required in the extraordinary circumstances of the ongoing war on Ukraine, serving as an important instrument to support critical investment in urban transport infrastructure and ensure uninterrupted provision of vital public transport services in the City of Mykolaiv. The latter is important for most vulnerable groups of population, including internally displaced persons (&#x2018;IDPs&#x2019;), and other concessionary passengers. 

The investment grant would also be instrumental to ensure the Project investment achieves maximum impact under existing affordability constraints in Ukraine. The Bank&#x2019;s investment supported by the Investment grant will enable the Company to make trolleybus operations more efficient through improved coverage and accessibility, increasing the average service speed, decreasing maintenance intensity and costs, and achieving energy savings and environmental benefits.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="275863" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment will supplement an on-going EBRD project (the &#x201c;Project&#x201d;) supporting (i) acquisition of low-floor trolleybuses with spare parts, maintenance and diagnostic equipment, (ii) rehabilitation and modernisation of an electric transport depot and (iii) traction power substations.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
